	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_group_icons">
		<text>Icons</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_group_counters">
		<text>Counters</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_group_fonts">
		<text>Appearance</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_enabled">
		<text>Enable L-CHUD</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_enabled_desc">
		<text>Turn the destination name and its counters on or off.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_detect_radius">
		<text>Detection Distance</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_detect_radius_desc">
		<text>How close you must be to a level transition before its destination can appear, in meters.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_detection_method">
		<text>Detection Method</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_detection_method_desc">
		<text>How the HUD decides that a level transition is in view. Auto uses Line of Sight on levels where another area sits above or below the transitions (Agroprom, Dark Valley, Yantar, Radar, both Chernobyl NPP levels, Generators, Jupiter, Zaton) and Simple everywhere else. Simple uses range and gaze alone and can show through walls. Line of Sight also requires that nothing solid (a wall, floor, ceiling) blocks the transition, which stops it from showing through geometry when another level area sits nearby in 3D space (e.g. an underground level directly below the surface).</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_detection_method_auto">
		<text>Auto</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_detection_method_simple">
		<text>Simple</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_detection_method_los">
		<text>Line of Sight</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_los_grace_ms">
		<text>Line of Sight Grace Period</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_los_grace_ms_desc">
		<text>How long a brief line-of-sight interruption (a branch, a rock edge, a corner) is ignored before the HUD hides, in milliseconds. Set to 0 to hide instantly on any interruption. Only used with Line of Sight detection.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_los_widen_radius_cm">
		<text>Line of Sight Target Radius</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_los_widen_radius_cm_desc">
		<text>Tolerate the line-of-sight check missing the transition's exact point by up to this distance, in centimeters, without moving the transition itself. Keep this modest: too large and the HUD can find a clear line through a nearby unrelated gap instead of the real one. Only used with Line of Sight detection.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_animation_view_angle">
		<text>Detection Angle</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_animation_view_angle_desc">
		<text>How closely you must look toward the transition. Higher values allow a wider viewing angle.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_drift_preset">
		<text>Animation Preset</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_drift_preset_desc">
		<text>How the destination label appears and disappears: fade timing, how far it rises, and how long the movement takes. Fade keeps the label still.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_elseform_lchud_drift_preset_instant">
